qsyn> tableau -h
Usage: tableau [-h] [list | new | delete | checkout | copy | append | adjoint | print | optimize] ...

Description:
  Tableau commands

Options:
  flag  -h, --help    show this help message 

Subcommands:
[list | new | delete | checkout | copy | append | adjoint | print | optimize]  
    list      List all Tableaus                         
    new       Create a new tableau                      
    delete    Delete a Tableau from the list            
    checkout  Checkout to Tableau with the ID specified 
    copy      Copy a Tableau                            
    append    Append a gate to a tableau                
    adjoint   transform the tableau to its adjoint      
    print     Print the tableau                         
    optimize  Optimize the tableau                      

qsyn> tableau o -h
Usage: tableau optimize [-h] (full | collapse | tmerge | hopt | unify | reorder | test | phasepoly | matpar) ...

Description:
  Optimize the tableau

Options:
  flag  -h, --help    show this help message 

Subcommands:
(full | collapse | tmerge | hopt | unify | reorder | test | phasepoly | matpar)  
    full       Perform tmerge, hopt, FastTODD until the T-count stops decreasing                                                                 
    collapse   Collapse the tableau into a canonical form                                                                                        
    tmerge     Merge rotations of the same rotation plane                                                                                        
    hopt       Minimize the number of Hadamard gates and internal Hadamard gates in the tableau                                                  
    unify      T-opt with H-gadgetize: gadgetize then FastTODD (no SMT reorder)                                                                  
    reorder    SMT-based gadget/PR reordering for ancilla minimization; runs unify first if needed                                               
    test       Run commute-text validation test and compare simulated PMC with ops section                                                       
    phasepoly  Reduce the number of terms for phase polynomials in the Tableau                                                                   
    matpar     partition the Pauli rotations into simultaneously-implementable tableaux. This option requires all Pauli rotations to be diagonal 

qsyn> tie-search -h
Usage: tie-search [-h] [--cycle [<size_t CYCLE>]] [--early-stop [<size_t EARLY-STOP>]] [-t-only | --t-only] ...

Description:
  runs the tie-search algorithm to co-optimize T and ancilla count. Measurement gates as well as ancilla will be added for optimization.

Options:
  flag    -h, --help                                           show this help message                                                                                                   
  size_t  --cycle, -cycle                          CYCLE       Optional safety cap on total phase-2 shots (default: unlimited)                                                          
  size_t  --early-stop, --early_stop, -early_stop  EARLY-STOP  Fixed tie-search patience override; all_random uses N/2 (default: dynamic max(60, ceil(2.5*A_min)) for the current best) 

Subcommands:
[-t-only | --t-only]  
    -t-only   Minimize T-count only (skip SMT/ancilla). Tracks last T-reduction step. 
    --t-only  Minimize T-count only (skip SMT/ancilla). Tracks last T-reduction step. 

qsyn> tableau o re
[error]    Tableau list is empty. Please create a Tableau first!!

qsyn> tie-search
[error]    QCir list is empty. Please create a QCir first!!
[error]    tie-search requires QCir; run qc read first

qsyn> quit -f

